    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Christian monarchy that united eastern and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#georgia">Georgia</a> in 1008 under the Bagratid dynasty.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#david-iv-of-georgia">David the Builder</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#tamar-of-georgia">Queen Tamar</a> it dominated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#caucasus">Caucasus</a> and enjoyed a golden age of poetry and church building.</li><li>Mongol conquest, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#timur">Timur</a>’s invasions and rebellious regional lords broke it into separate kingdoms by 1490.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#david-iv-of-georgia">David the Builder</a> settled thousands of Kipchak families from the steppes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#georgia">Georgia</a> as soldiers, and Tamar was crowned with the title of king rather than queen.</p></aside>
    </section>

